<title>CHINA: China boasts 10 percent gain from corn fertiliser.</title>
<headline>China boasts 10 percent gain from corn fertiliser.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has developed a fertiliser that can boost corn output by more than 10 percent, the Economic Daily said on Friday.</p>
<p>The fertiliser, developed by the Chinese Academy of Sciences, the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Chemical Industry, was tested on 5,336 hectares of summer corn, it said.</p>
<p>Results showed the fertiliser boosted production by 600-750 kg per hectare, it said.</p>
<p>China's annual corn output in 1995 was 101 million tonnes and has been forecast to reach 128.95 million tonnes in 2000.</p>
</text>
